    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6426" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cāmus</span></b> , i, m., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κημός</span> (Dor. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καμός</span>). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A muzzle</i> for horses (only in eccl. Lat.), <i><span class="en">Vulg. Psa.
				31, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ambros. Hex. 6,
			3</span></i>.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Perh. <i>a kind of collar for the neck</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Non. p. 200, 16</span></i> (Trag. Rel. v.
			302 Rib.).</div> ‡† <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cana</span></b> , Gr. (*<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάνεον</span>, plur.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάνεα κάνη</span>, a wicker basket) for
		canistra, acc. to Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p. 45</span></i> Müll.</div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
